tect the  anonymity of that victim  john doe one is a u.s resident  as a result of this conduct which  occurred over a period of years  unfortunately  and involved operational activity from  coast to coast and around the tri-state  area  we charged eight defendants five of them  uh  were arrested uh this morning  um as alleged in the complaint which  uh there's much more detail in the  complaint i'm just gonna do my best to  summarize that a little bit  complaint on file is over 40 pages and  it's it's rich with facts but  essentially what it says is that over a  three-year period  members of the prc government directed  several individuals to engage in  unsanctioned  and illegal conduct in the united states  on behalf of the people's republic of  china  for the purpose of coercing a person  john doe one  to return to the people's republic of  china  we believe they did so because john doe  won and another victim his spouse  are alleged by the chinese government to  have committed some violations of  chinese law but rather than go through  the appropriate channels with the u.s  government to pursue those charges  prc officials and these defendants in  this case  engaged in extrajudicial conduct that  really violates not only u.s  law but the types of norms and  principles of comedy that we would  expect  from a foreign government the charge  conspiracy involved  efforts to pressure john doe one  directly  and also by taking actions that affected  his family members  including his wife his adult daughter  and other family members who resided in  the united states and some who resided  overseas in china  the effort was sustained relentless over  years  it involved some discrete acts to  frighten intimidate and coerce john doe  and it involved some  shockingly overt act it involves  surveillance including  we believe with the use of night vision  goggles involved leaving threatening  notes on the victim's doors  and i think perhaps most distressingly  uh targeting  the victim's daughter the efforts also  involve  seeking the assistance of a us-based  private investigator  to bend him to the will of this unlawful  mission  um to get into just a few of the  specifics  one of the notes read you know for  example quote if you are willing to go  back to the mainland  and spend 10 years in prison your wife  and children will be safe and all right  that's the end of the matter this is  conduct  we would not tolerate from our own  citizens  certainly not from our own officials it  constitutes  stalking and it is certainly not conduct  that we will tolerate  when conducted unilaterally by a foreign  government  with no notice and without the  permission of the united states  government  that is in summon substance what this  case is about  that's what led us to take what i  believe to be unprecedented action  to enforce the rule of law and  it's it's unacceptable and it and it  will not be permitted to continue  it's important i think also to note that  our investigation continues  and also to remind people once again  that these defendants like all  defendants are entitled  to their day in court today they look  forward to the burden to prove their  guilt is on us  and we embrace that burden i i just want  to echo  the the sentiment of director wray  where this a case like this really does  take a whole of government  uh approach we've had great partnership  with the fbi the national security  division  we got a critical assistance from the  department of homeland security and the  department of state  and our colleagues in the u.s attorney  community across the country  who really stood shoulder to shoulder  with us to enforce the rule of law  in this case is in all other cases so  thank you for the opportunity this  morning it's it's my understanding  that some questions now from the media  will be directed  to us thank you  we will now begin the question and  answer session to ask a question  you may press star then 1 on your  touchstone phone  if you are using a speakerphone please  pick up your handset before pressing the  keys  to withdraw your question please press  star then too  please specify who your question should  go to when your line is open  and limit yourself to one question you  may  return to the question queue with  additional questions at this time we'll  pause momentarily to assemble the roster  the first question comes from aruna  siswanatha  please go ahead from the wall street  journal  hi thanks for doing this so as you  mentioned  i think uh john timmers mentioned this  has been going on since  2014 and this is the first time you have  uh brought some cases here  is there have you seen an escalation in  um these kinds of harassment efforts  over the past  year or two or what kind of change have  you seen  are they being more aggressive about  targeting these people  our understanding is there are at least  two dozen sort of publicly identified  targets in the u.s  so i don't know that i could give you a  quantitative assessment  of the trend but i think it's fair to  say that this is  as i said in my opening remarks far from  an isolated incident  that's become all too common not just  here in the united states but  in a number of other countries around  the world who also respect the rule of  law  and some of the conduct that we've seen  here is  really beyond the pale and needs to be  stopped in the most firm manner possible  the next question comes from pete  williams of nbc news  please go ahead thank you mr ray where  were these folks arrested and  were they ever successful in getting  people to go back to china  uh well i'll i'll let uh uh seth speak  to  uh the last part uh but we uh had people  working both in our new haven  new york newark and los angeles field  offices  on the operation that took place this  morning  seth sure if i can  just add to that i think uh one of our  five defendants  was arrested in new jersey um  two were arrested in new york this  morning and uh  two others were arrested in california  [Music]  fortunately in this case as you know as  the facts we've  alleged set forth we were able to  essentially  uh protect the victim from intimidation  and and i can't really go beyond the  scope of what's in the public record  with respect to  other instances in which uh the chinese  agents may or may not have been  successful in their efforts but  unfortunately in this case we've been  able to protect the victims  the next question comes from nick  schifrin from pbs  please go ahead thanks for doing this  can you  discuss who the five who you've arrested  are who you believe they were working  for and how they entered  the united states whether they lied on  any visa applications and you've  mentioned xi jinping  multiple times i can imagine that you  have connections  to these people to prc officials  but do you have personal uh evidence or  evidence that xi jinping personally was  involved  so so this is that i'm not sure who the  question was directed to but  i can talk about the defendants a little  bit  so with respect to the five defendants  who were arrested today  just briefly uh hungarian was a  30 year old naturalized u.s citizen  he resided in queens new york jyn  participated  in the scheme to stalk our victim john  doe won  in or about april of 2017 by assisting  with the travel lunch and logistics  planning for zhufang  and some prc officials as well as  assisting with the surveillance  on john doe one and his father  with respect to ju young  i can tell you that yang  who's also known as jason zhu he's a 64  year old prc citizen  and a legal permanent resident of the  united states he resides in flushing new  york  he was involved in hiring the the  private investigator michael mcmahon  to help investigate and surveil and  ultimately stalk  john de juan on behalf of the prc  government  um michael mcmahon is a 53 year old u.s  citizen he's a licensed private  detective in new jersey  and he was essentially recruited and  hired to assist with surveillance and  conducting other aspects of the  operation  rong zhing is a 38 year old u.s legal  permanent  resident and prc citizen he resides in  california  his role essentially was seeking  location information  for people in the united states on  behalf of the prc government  and then with respect to the fifth  defendant who was arrested today  zhang ying  he's a 24 year old prc citizen  and a legal permanent resident  zhang resides in brooklyn during the  relevant time period at least and  now he resides out in california where  he was arrested  earlier this morning so hopefully that  that's some helpful background on the  defendants  and responsive to your question thank  you  the next question comes from eric tucker  from the associated press  please go ahead hi thank you so much for  doing this i was wondering and this  question may again be for for seth or  for john  um i was wondering if you could talk a  little bit about what the  value to the prc was or the individuals  who were being targeted what was it  about  them and their backgrounds that led um  to this very aggressive and illegal  pursuit  were they themselves sort of active  dissonance of the prc or was there  something else that made them so  significant to the government  thank you thanks very much eric i think  you know we don't want to go further  into why these specific individuals were  targeted were very keen  to protect their identities and  obviously any information that we give  along those lines could be used to  uh reconstruct who these folks were so i  think we'll leave it as what was in the  indictment  with of course the overlay i think as  your question recognizes that  while some individuals are legitimately  sought  for criminal activity although  in an illegitimate way others in fact  are  dissidents critics rivals of  the chinese general secretary thanks  this now concludes the press conference  you may now disconnect  yo